### Task 3: the writer option and the cover judge-copy helper (D4, D9)

Commit `ded5d5ff21f338ff301cbadfab0f71e2a22bbec4`, message
`feat(storytime_l2_retries_cover): the approvalsOnly option and the cover judge copies`.

The option `approvalsOnly` is false by default. When it is true, the writer delivers only the rows
of the approval list. A row without an entry gets no job, the reuse rows stay out of the
delivery, and `onSkip` stays quiet. The pin check, the check of each entry against the list, and
the file checks stay.

The helper `scripts/storytime-cover-judge-copy.mjs` writes the clean copy at 1448 x 2048 px and the
copy with the zone lines at 20, 29, 30, 78, 88, and 94 percent of the height. The rows are 410,
594, 614, 1597, 1802, and 1925. The judge brief lists the 12 checks and the form of the result.

